          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            7. What Do Buyers Say About Super Mass Gainer Taste and Mixing?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Buyers mostly report that Super Mass Gainer tastes sweet and dessert-like and mixes better than they expected for such a large serving, while the most common complaints are bloating, gas and the sheer volume of the shake. We have not tasted it, so the points below summarise patterns in retailer reviews and the claims on Dymatize's page rather than our own experience.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Flavor</h3>

          <p>
            Rich Chocolate and Gourmet Vanilla are the two long-running flavors, and reviewers often describe both as rich and milkshake-like, especially mixed with milk. Fruity Pebbles, made under license from Post, divides opinion more: fans of the cereal flavor like it, while others find it very sweet at this serving size. Our <a href="/fruity-pebbles-protein-powder/">Fruity Pebbles protein powder guide</a> compares it with the ISO100 version, which has a fraction of the calories.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Mixing and volume</h3>

          <p>
            Dymatize says the powder blends easily and works for baking. The practical problem is volume: 2 1/2 cups of powder in 24 oz of liquid is a big shake, and a standard 20 oz shaker will not hold it. Buyers commonly recommend a blender or a large shaker, adding the liquid first, and splitting the serving. Some report clumps when the powder goes in first or when the bag is near its end and the powder has settled.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Stomach and complaints</h3>

          <p>
            The most frequent complaint about any big gainer, this one included, is digestive: bloating, gas and a heavy, overly full feeling, especially after a full 1,280-calorie serving. Lactose from the whey concentrate, a large fast dose of maltodextrin and the gums can all play a part. Starting at a quarter or half serving for a week usually helps. Other complaints buyers raise are the large scoop count per bag, broken bag seals and the sweetness of the flavors.
          </p>
        </div>

