        <div id="is-it-healthy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            9. Is Dymatize Super Mass Gainer Healthy?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Super Mass Gainer is a reasonable tool for people who truly need extra calories, but it is not a health food, and for anyone who already eats enough it mainly adds fat. About 980 of its 1,280 calories come from carbohydrate, mostly maltodextrin, a fast-digesting starch with a high glycemic index. It has no fiber in Vanilla and 14 g of added sugar, which is 28% of the Daily Value in one shake.
          </p>

          <p>
            Against that, it provides 52 g of complete milk protein, 950 mg of calcium and a spread of B vitamins and vitamin C, and its fat and saturated fat are modest at 10 g and 2.5 g. For an underweight adult lifter, a person recovering lost weight under medical guidance, or someone with a very small appetite, those calories can be easier to get from a shake than from food.
          </p>

          <p>
            The &quot;clean&quot; question depends on your definition. Super Mass Gainer contains sucralose, acesulfame potassium, artificial flavors, carrageenan and soy lecithin. None of these is banned, and regulators allow them, but people who avoid artificial sweeteners or carrageenan will prefer Naked Mass or a homemade shake. Our <a href="/best-protein-powder-without-artificial-sweeteners/">protein powder without artificial sweeteners guide</a> has more options.
          </p>

          <p>
            Over the long run, a liquid surplus built mostly on maltodextrin can push weight gain toward fat rather than muscle if you are not training hard. Track your waist measurement along with your weight. If your waist grows faster than your lifts improve, cut to a half serving or replace the gainer with food.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">HEALTH CAVEAT</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Check with a professional first if this applies to you</p>
            <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed m-0">Super Mass Gainer delivers about 245 g of carbohydrate and 52 g of protein in one shake. Talk to a doctor or registered dietitian before using it if you have diabetes or prediabetes, kidney disease, a heart condition, a milk or soy allergy, are pregnant or breastfeeding, take medication, are under 18, or are an older adult with a medical condition. This page is not medical advice.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div id="who-should-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Buy Dymatize Super Mass Gainer, and Who Should Skip It?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Super Mass Gainer suits adults who are underweight or naturally lean, train with weights and cannot eat enough food to gain, and who want the most calories per dollar. If you have tried bigger meals and still cannot gain, a half serving a day is a simple, cheap way to add about 640 calories without cooking or extra chewing.
          </p>

          <p>
            It also suits people with irregular schedules, such as shift workers or students, who miss meals and need a fast calorie source they can mix in a minute. The 12 lb bag at about $4.37 per full serving, or about $2.19 per half serving, is cheaper than most fast food meals with similar calories and has far more protein.
          </p>

          <p>
            Skip it if your goal is simply more protein. A whey concentrate or isolate gives 25 g of protein in 120 to 150 calories, and our <a href="/dymatize-protein-powder-review/">Dymatize protein powder review</a> covers Elite 100% Whey and ISO100 for that job. Skip it too if you are already at a healthy weight and want to lean bulk, if you are drug-tested and need a verifiable certification, or if you have a medical reason to limit carbohydrate or sugar.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you want more calories without a gainer, start with food: whole milk, oats, nut butter, rice, olive oil and an extra meal before bed. Add a regular protein powder to fill the protein gap. If that still leaves you short, a gainer earns its place. Our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-weight-gain/">best protein powder for weight gain</a> guide ranks gainers and high-calorie proteins side by side, including leaner options such as Pro Gainer that give 60 g of protein in about 650 calories.
          </p>
        </div>

