        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            11. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Drinking the full 1,280-calorie serving from day one</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Jumping straight to 2 1/2 cups of powder is the fastest route to bloating, gas and a shake you abandon. Start with a quarter or half serving for the first week, watch how your stomach responds, and only work up to the full serving if your weight gain stalls.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Using it as an everyday protein shake</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Super Mass Gainer is a calorie product. If you eat enough already and drink it after every workout for protein, you add about 980 calories of carbohydrate a day and mostly gain fat. A regular whey powder does that job with roughly a tenth of the calories.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Relying on its 1 g of creatine</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The Amazon listing gives 1 g of creatine per serving, about a fifth of the 3 to 5 g daily dose most studies use. Treat it as a bonus, not a creatine supplement. If you want creatine benefits, add a separate scoop of creatine monohydrate.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting the testing icon if you are drug-tested</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Dymatize's Banned Substance Tested claim does not name the certifier, so it cannot be checked against a registry. Athletes subject to testing should confirm the program with Dymatize and search that program's database for this exact product before using it.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Mixing it in a small shaker with powder first</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Two and a half cups of powder will not fit a standard shaker with 24 oz of liquid, and powder poured first tends to clump at the bottom. Use a blender or a large shaker, pour the liquid in first, and split the serving if needed.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
